var e=JSON.parse('[{"id":"we-01","title":"Troubleshooting USB File Copy Failure (\'File is too large for the destination file system\') & FAT32 to NTFS Conversion","problemStatement":"Ek user ke paas 64 GB ka USB flash drive hai jismein 50 GB free space available hai. Jab user ek 4.7 GB size ki Windows 11 installation ISO image file ko USB drive par copy karne ki koshish karta hai, toh Windows error dialog deta hai: \'The file is too large for the destination file system.\' Is error ka exact cause identify karo aur bina data erase kiye command-line se drive ko compatible format mein convert karne ka step-by-step solution provide karo.","input":"File Size = 4.7 GB; USB Free Space = 50 GB; USB File System = FAT32; Target File System = NTFS","difficulty":"Intermediate","concept":"FAT32 4 GB File Size Limit & Non-Destructive File System Conversion","steps":[{"stepNumber":1,"action":"Error ka root cause diagnose karo","detail":"USB drive ka current file system FAT32 hai. FAT32 file system mein individual file length field 32-bit unsigned integer hoti hai, isliye single file ka maximum representable size 2^32 - 1 Bytes = 4,294,967,295 Bytes (exactly 4 GB - 1 Byte) hota hai.\\nKyunki ISO file ka size 4.7 GB hai (> 4 GB), isliye chahe USB drive par 50 GB free space ho, FAT32 architecture is file ko physically allocate nahi kar sakti."},{"stepNumber":2,"action":"Solution approach select karo","detail":"File system ko NTFS ya exFAT mein convert karna hoga kyunki NTFS aur exFAT dono multiple Terabytes ki single files support karte hain.\\nWindows command-line utility `convert` use karke bina existing files delete kiye FAT32 drive ko direct NTFS mein convert kiya ja sakta hai."},{"stepNumber":3,"action":"Command Prompt ko Administrator mode mein launch karo","detail":"Start Menu mein \'cmd\' type karo -> Right-click -> \'Run as administrator\' select karo."},{"stepNumber":4,"action":"Conversion command execute karo","detail":"Agar USB drive letter \'E:\' hai, toh command execute karo:\\n`convert E: /fs:ntfs`\\nWindows drive integrity check karega aur existing files ko preserve karte hue file system table ko NTFS mein migrate kar dega."},{"stepNumber":5,"action":"File copy operation retry karo","detail":"Conversion complete hone ke baad USB drive NTFS format mein aa jati hai. 4.7 GB ISO file ko successfully copy kiya ja sakta hai bina kisi error ke."}],"output":"Drive converted from FAT32 to NTFS; 4.7 GB ISO file successfully copied; Existing drive data preserved.","verification":"NTFS max file size limit 16 TB hai jo 4.7 GB se hazaro guna badi hai. Non-destructive `convert` utility successfully verified."},{"id":"we-02","title":"Effective Network Permissions Evaluation on Shared Folder (Share vs NTFS Most Restrictive Rule)","problemStatement":"Windows Server par ek folder `D:\\\\CompanyData` network par share kiya gaya hai jiska share name `CompanyData` hai. Security administrator ne folder par do alag permission layers configure ki hain:\\n1. Share Permissions: User \'Rahul\' ke liye \'Read\' permission di gayi hai.\\n2. NTFS Permissions: User \'Rahul\' ke liye \'Full Control\' permission di gayi hai.\\nCalculate karo: (a) Jab Rahul local computer par physically login karega toh uski effective permission kya hogi? (b) Jab Rahul network ke zariye `\\\\\\\\Server\\\\CompanyData` access karega toh uski effective permission kya hogi?","input":"User = Rahul; Share Permission = Read; NTFS Permission = Full Control; Access Methods = Local vs Network","difficulty":"Intermediate","concept":"Windows Access Control Evaluation & Most Restrictive Precedence Invariant","steps":[{"stepNumber":1,"action":"Scenario (a): Local Physical Logon access evaluate karo","detail":"Rule: Jab koi user computer par locally physical console se login karta hai, toh **Share Permissions completely bypass** ho jati hain (Share permissions sirf network stack par exist karti hain).\\nLocal logon par sirf aur sirf **NTFS Permissions** evaluate hoti hain.\\nNTFS Permission = Full Control.\\nIsliye local access par Rahul ko **Full Control (Read, Write, Modify, Delete, Change Permissions)** milti hai."},{"stepNumber":2,"action":"Scenario (b): Network Access permission layers evaluate karo","detail":"Rule: Jab user network path (`\\\\\\\\Server\\\\CompanyData`) ke zariye folder access karta hai, toh Windows dono permission sets evaluate karta hai:\\nShare Permission = Read\\nNTFS Permission = Full Control."},{"stepNumber":3,"action":"Most Restrictive Precedence rule apply karo","detail":"Formula: Effective Network Permission = Most Restrictive of (Share Permission, NTFS Permission).\\n\'Read\' aur \'Full Control\' mein se sabse zyada restrictive (sakht) permission \'Read\' hai.\\nIsliye network level par Share permission ek strict bottleneck filter ki tarah kaam karti hai."},{"stepNumber":4,"action":"Final permissions summarize karo","detail":"Network ke zariye Rahul sirf files read aur open kar sakta hai; woh koi nayi file create ya existing file edit/delete nahi kar sakta."}],"output":"Local Access Effective Permission: Full Control; Network Access Effective Permission: Read only.","verification":"Windows Access Token evaluation engine hamesha network access par token intersection evaluate karta hai: Read ∩ Full Control = Read. Verified!"},{"id":"we-03","title":"MBR Partition Table Capacity Limit Calculation & GPT Partitioning Migration for 4 TB Drive","problemStatement":"Ek system administrator ne desktop computer mein nayi 4 TB (4,000 GB) capacity ki physical hard disk install ki. Administrator ne use legacy Master Boot Record (MBR) partition style mein initialize kiya aur 2 TB ka ek partition create kiya. Lekin baaki bache hue 2 TB unallocated space par jab administrator new volume banane ki koshish karta hai, toh options greyed out (disabled) aate hain. Explain karo ki MBR mein yeh limitation kyun aati hai aur disk ko 100% capacity use karne ke liye kaise configure karein.","input":"Physical Drive = 4 TB; Current Partition Style = MBR; Target Partition Style = GPT","difficulty":"Intermediate","concept":"MBR 32-bit Sector Addressing Arithmetic & GPT Migration","steps":[{"stepNumber":1,"action":"MBR 32-bit mathematical limit calculate karo","detail":"MBR partition table format mein LBA (Logical Block Addressing) sector address store karne ke liye strictly 32-bit field hoti hai.\\nStandard hard drive sector size = 512 Bytes = 2^9 Bytes.\\nMaximum addressable sectors = 2^32 sectors = 4,294,967,296 sectors.\\nMaximum addressable capacity = 2^32 × 512 Bytes = 2^41 Bytes = 2,199,023,255,552 Bytes = exactly 2.0 TB (approx 2.2 TB in decimal metric).\\nIs 2 TB limit ke aage ka koi bhi sector MBR table mathematically address hi nahi kar sakti."},{"stepNumber":2,"action":"Remaining 2 TB unusable hone ka reason formulate karo","detail":"4 TB hard disk mein se pehla 2 TB MBR ke range mein aata hai, jabki agla 2 TB space 32-bit sector addressing boundary ke bahar chala jata hai. Isliye Disk Management use unallocated dikhata hai par uspar koi partition banane ki permission nahi deta."},{"stepNumber":3,"action":"GPT (GUID Partition Table) solution select karo","detail":"GPT 64-bit sector addressing use karta hai aur 9.4 Zettabytes (9.4 × 10^21 Bytes) tak support karta hai. GPT mein 4 TB disk ka 100% space fully accessible ho jata hai."},{"stepNumber":4,"action":"Conversion steps perform karo","detail":"Disk Management (`diskmgmt.msc`) open karo -> Disk par bane 2 TB volume ko delete karo (disk empty honi chahiye) -> Disk number label par Right-Click karo -> \'Convert to GPT Disk\' select karo -> Ab poore 4 TB space par chahe single 4 TB volume banao ya multiple partitions."}],"output":"Reason: MBR 32-bit sector limit (2^32 × 512B = 2 TB); Solution: Convert to GPT Partition Table; Result: Full 4 TB capacity utilized.","verification":"GPT sector addresses are 64-bit: 2^64 × 512B = 9.4 ZB. 4 TB is easily handled within GPT specifications."},{"id":"we-04","title":"Device Manager Hardware Driver Diagnostic & Rollback Workflow","problemStatement":"Windows 10 computer mein graphics card ka new driver update hone ke baad screen resolution corrupt ho jati hai aur display flicker karne lagti hai. Device Manager open karne par Display Adapters category mein graphic card ke icon par ek yellow exclamation mark (!) dikhai deta hai. Device Manager symbol ka exact meaning explain karo aur display ko previous stable state mein lane ke troubleshooting steps execute karo.","input":"Symptom = Display flickering after driver update; Symbol = Yellow Exclamation Mark (!) on Display Adapter","difficulty":"Easy","concept":"Device Manager Status Indicators & Driver Roll Back Technique","steps":[{"stepNumber":1,"action":"Device Manager open karo aur symbol identify karo","detail":"Keyboard par `Win + X` press karke \'Device Manager\' choose karo (ya Run box mein `devmgmt.msc` type karo).\\nDisplay Adapters expand karne par graphics card par Yellow Exclamation Mark (!) dikhta hai.\\nYellow Exclamation Mark (!) ka meaning: Hardware physically detect hua hai lekin installed device driver corrupted hai, incompatible hai, ya hardware start hone mein fail ho raha hai (Error Code 43/10)."},{"stepNumber":2,"action":"Device Properties open karo","detail":"Yellow exclamation mark wale graphic card par Right-Click karo -> \'Properties\' select karo -> \'General\' tab mein Device Status check karo jo driver failure indicate karega."},{"stepNumber":3,"action":"\'Driver\' tab par jao aur \'Roll Back Driver\' execute karo","detail":"\'Driver\' tab select karo. Wahan 5 options hote hain: Driver Details, Update Driver, Roll Back Driver, Disable Device, Uninstall Device.\\nKyunki issue new update ke baad aaya hai, isliye **\'Roll Back Driver\'** button par click karo.\\nWindows puchega: \'Why are you rolling back?\' -> Reason select karke \'Yes\' confirm karo."},{"stepNumber":4,"action":"System verification aur driver restoration","detail":"Windows current faulty driver ko uninstall karega aur previous working backup driver files ko restore kar dega. Screen ek baar blink hogi aur normal native resolution restore ho jayegi. Yellow exclamation mark hat jayega."}],"output":"Yellow Exclamation Mark diagnosed as driver failure; Roll Back Driver restored previous stable driver; Display resolution fixed.","verification":"Device status in Device Manager now reads: \'This device is working properly.\' Exclamation icon disappears."},{"id":"we-05","title":"Windows Registry Modification, REG_DWORD Value Configuration & .reg Backup Restoration","problemStatement":"System administrator ko Windows 10/11 machines par USB Storage Devices ke write access ko block karna hai taaki data theft roka ja sake. Administrator ko Registry Editor (`regedit`) mein jakar `StorageDevicePolicies` key ke andar `WriteProtect` parameter set karna hai. Explain karo: (1) Kaunsa root hive use hoga, (2) Kaunsa data type use hoga aur value kya hogi, aur (3) Safety ke liye backup kaise liya jata hai.","input":"Target Policy = Disable USB write access; Tool = regedit; Setting Name = WriteProtect","difficulty":"Intermediate","concept":"Windows Registry Hives, REG_DWORD Configuration & .reg File Import/Export","steps":[{"stepNumber":1,"action":"Appropriate Root Hive select karo","detail":"Kyunki yeh setting computer ke sabhi users par globally apply honi chahiye, isliye **HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE (HKLM)** hive select kiya jata hai (machine-wide settings HKLM mein hoti hain, HKCU mein nahi)."},{"stepNumber":2,"action":"Safety Backup (.reg file) export karo","detail":"Kisi bhi key ko modify karne se pehle safety mandatory practice hai: Registry Editor menu mein File -> Export select karo -> \'Export range: All\' ya selected branch choose karke file ko `backup_registry.reg` naam se save karo."},{"stepNumber":3,"action":"Registry path navigate karo","detail":"Path navigate karo:\\n`HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\\\SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Control\\\\StorageDevicePolicies`\\nAgar `StorageDevicePolicies` key exist na kare toh Control par right-click karke New -> Key banate hain."},{"stepNumber":4,"action":"New REG_DWORD value create karke configure karo","detail":"Right pane mein empty space par Right-Click karo -> New -> **DWORD (32-bit) Value** (REG_DWORD) select karo.\\nValue Name: `WriteProtect` enter karo.\\n`WriteProtect` par double-click karo aur Value Data: `1` (Enable write protection) set karo. Base: Hexadecimal/Decimal (dono mein 1 hi hota hai)."},{"stepNumber":5,"action":"Restoration procedure verify karo","detail":"Agar future mein USB write protection hatana ho, toh ya toh value ko `0` set karo, ya created `backup_registry.reg` file par double-click karke original settings wapas merge kar do."}],"output":"Hive: HKLM; Data Type: REG_DWORD; Value: 1 (Write Protection Active); Backup: .reg export file created.","verification":"Plugging in a USB drive and attempting to save a file produces \'The disk is write-protected\' error. Verified!"},{"id":"we-06","title":"System Restore Point Execution Trace & Personal File Invariance Verification","problemStatement":"Ek accountant ke computer mein Accounting Software update hone ke baad database driver crash hone lagta hai. Accountant 3 din pehle banaye gaye Restore Point par System Restore (`rstrui.exe`) run karne ka faisla karta hai. Lekin accountant ko chinta hai ki pichle 3 dino mein banaye gaye 15 naye Excel accounting spreadsheets aur client emails delete ho jayenge. System Restore execution flow explain karo aur clarify karo ki personal files ke sath kya hota hai.","input":"Disaster Scenario = Corrupted driver update after accounting software upgrade; Tool = System Restore (rstrui.exe)","difficulty":"Easy","concept":"System Restore Mechanics, Volume Shadow Copy & Personal Data Invariance","steps":[{"stepNumber":1,"action":"System Restore tool launch karo","detail":"Win + R press karke `rstrui.exe` (ya `rstrui`) run karo, ya System Properties -> \'System Protection\' tab -> \'System Restore\' par click karo."},{"stepNumber":2,"action":"Available Restore Points browse karo","detail":"System Restore wizard open hoga. \'Choose a different restore point\' select karo. List mein se 3 din pehle create hua Automatic Restore Point (e.g. \'Windows Update\' ya \'System Scheduled\') select karo."},{"stepNumber":3,"action":"\'Scan for affected programs\' check karo","detail":"\'Scan for affected programs\' button par click karo. Windows scan karke batayega ki kaunse software updates aur device drivers rollback honge (accounting software driver restore hoga)."},{"stepNumber":4,"action":"Personal files safety invariance verify karo","detail":"System Restore Volume Shadow Copy (VSS) architecture use karta hai jo sirf system files (`.dll`, `.sys`, `.exe`), Windows Registry hives, aur system environment variables ko monitor karta hai.\\nUser profile directory (`C:\\\\Users\\\\Accountant\\\\Documents\\\\`, `Desktop\\\\`, `Pictures\\\\`, `Downloads\\\\`) ke personal data files (`.xlsx`, `.docx`, `.pdf`, `.pst` email databases) ko System Restore touch **NAHI** karta."},{"stepNumber":5,"action":"System Restore complete karo aur verify karo","detail":"System restart hota hai aur registry rollback ho jati hai. Boot hone ke baad: Accounting driver stable state mein aa jata hai aur pichle 3 dino ki saari 15 Excel spreadsheets Desktop aur Documents folder mein 100% intact aur untouched milti hain."}],"output":"System files and registry rolled back 3 days; Accounting software functional; All 15 personal Excel files completely safe.","verification":"System Restore architecture strictly excludes user library directories. Zero data loss verified."}]');export{e as default};